  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Structure**\n\nI\'m currently examining the project directory structure. I\'ve noted the existing files: `metadata.json`, `index.html`, `src/App.tsx`, `package.json`, and `vite.config.ts`. My immediate priority is to scrutinize `metadata.json` and adjust the \"name\" and \"description\" fields according to the given instructions. I\'ll maintain the existing permissions and capabilities defined within the file.\n\n\n**Incorporating Fonts and Metatags**\n\nI\'ve moved on to integrating the appropriate fonts and syncing metatags. I\'m focusing on Ol Chiki, Warang Chiti, and Devanagari scripts, using \"Noto Sans\" and \"Baloo 2\" from Google Fonts. I\'m also ensuring the HTML\'s title and description match the `metadata.json` file.\n\n\n**Defining Project Specifications**\n\nMy analysis has evolved, focusing now on the user prompt\'s detailed requirements. \"Noto Sans Warang Chiti\" and \"Noto Sans Devanagari\" offer a fitting \"children\'s cartoon textbook\" vibe. I\'m now developing the specifications, which will include multi-language support (Santali, Ho, and Mundari) as described, along with script options and language-specific content storage. I\'m also considering the extensibility for Kurukh, Khortha, and Nag.\n\n\n**Defining Curriculum Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided curriculum details. Specifically, I plan to incorporate JCERT textbooks from Classes 1 to 5. I\'ve noted the structure and names of the books and chapters, including those for Maths, Hindi (\"\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262\"), and English (\"Marigold\"/\"Sunshine\"). The proposed bridge toggle (\"Mother Tongue | Hindi | English\") is straightforward to add. I\'ll maintain the focus on the specified languages and script options.\n\n\n**Mapping Curriculum Data**\n\nI\'m currently working to map the curriculum data for Classes 2 through 5. I\'ve broken down the content, noting chapter titles like \"\340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276 \340\244\271\340\245\210 \340\244\262\340\244\202\340\244\254\340\244\276, \340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276 \340\244\271\340\245\210 \340\244\227\340\245\213\340\244\262?\" and \"\340\244\252\340\245\202\340\244\250\340\244\256 \340\244\225\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\244\232\340\244\260\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276,\" across Maths and EVS subjects. I\'m focusing on the structure and content for each class level.\n\n\n**Defining User Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interactions and the application\'s flow. I\'m designing a welcome screen with an animated mascot (\"Birsa\" or \"Chotu\") and audio greetings in the target languages. I\'m creating language choice cards with illustrations and native script representations for Santali, Ho, and Mundari. I\'ll implement audio feedback on hover/tap for class selection (e.g., Elephant for Class 1). A well-defined JSON schema or data file (`curriculum.json` or within `src/data`) for the curriculum data, including translation capabilities, is now a priority, with the first Math chapter of class 1 as the benchmark.\n\n\n**Defining Lesson Interaction**\n\nI\'m now expanding the user flow with detailed lesson interactions. I\'ve designed selection steps: Class selection (Elephant for Class 1, Deer for Class 2, Tiger for Class 3, Rhinoceros for Class 5), subject choice with sound on tap for Maths, Hindi, EVS, and English. The chapter selection will be an adventure map with numbered steps and illustrations. The lesson screen will display explanations, native script and transliteration with a bridge toggle for Hindi/English. I\'ll include audio narration with highlighted text. Animated content, interactive games, and an \"Ask Chotu\" AI button will be incorporated.\n\n\n**Designing Interactions**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing interaction details. I\'m focusing on \"Chotu\", the chatbot, which will be a multilingual cartoon character. I\'m also thinking through rewards, like stars, badges, and a sticker book. Additionally, UI elements like a high contrast mode and reduce motion setting are coming into focus, plus sound toggles and responsive audio cues.\n\n\n**Defining Quality Control**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring quality and providing review mechanisms. I\'ve designed status badges: \"teacher-reviewed\", \"approved\", and \"AI draft.\" I\'m including a \"report wrong translation\" feature. A glossary for each language, covering school terms, is a new addition.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'ve moved on to the teacher/admin panel. I\'m imagining a teacher login (maybe a quick passkey). This will give access to a review queue, allowing draft edits, approvals/rejections, and audio upload capabilities. I plan to include an analytics dashboard to display chapters completed, game scores and common mistakes. I can also foresee an export functionality for the approved translations dataset.\n\n\n"
