  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing App Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the app\'s architecture based on the user\'s specs. I\'ve begun mapping out the data schema, starting with the core components: Class (1-5), Subject (\"maths,\" \"hindi,\" etc.), and Book Name (e.g., \"\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202\"). This foundation will guide the structure of the app, ensuring a logical flow for the educational content.\n\n\n**Refining Content Structure**\n\nI\'ve significantly refined the content structure. I\'m now drilling down to chapter details, considering multiple languages: Santali (Ol Chiki), Ho (Warang Chiti), and Mundari (Devanagari). For each chapter and language, I\'m defining titles, script text, transliterations, and detailed lesson content including sentences, illustrations, audio cues, and key vocabulary. This granular level of planning aims for a rich, multilingual educational experience.\n\n\n**Defining Content Metadata**\n\nI\'m now detailing metadata within each chapter for a richer interactive experience. This includes audio and video integration via URLs, game configurations for activities, and review statuses with reviewer details. The plan involves adding review data for each section. I\'m structuring review details as \"approved\", \"teacher-reviewed\", or \"ai-draft\", alongside the reviewer\'s name and feedback. This will improve collaborative review workflows.\n\n\n**Defining Language Profiles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining detailed language profiles. I\'ve fleshed out the \'Ho Jagar\' language entry, detailing its script name (Warang Chiti), alternative names, font class, and available scripts (including Devanagari and Roman). I\'m also adding its greeting text and associated audio, flag color, icon, and description. I\'m doing the same for Mundari, with similar detail. This ensures robust multilingual support within the app.\n\n\n**Expanding Language Support**\n\nI\'m expanding the language support with a focus on demonstrably extensibility. I\'ve integrated an icon emoji and a new description for Mundari. I\'m also planning to include Kurukh and Khortha with a \"Coming Soon\" preview. I\'m defining bridge language options for easy switching between mother-tongue, Hindi, English, and bilingual modes. I\'m also working on developing an audio engine for sound effects and native speech narration using the SpeechSynthesis API.\n\n\n**Implementing Narration Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating playback controls for audio narration. I\'ve got \"play,\" \"pause,\" and \"restart\" functionalities in sync with the current word/phrase. This will greatly improve the user experience for auditory learners.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Games**\n\nI\'m now designing interactive games for engagement! I\'m planning a \"Big vs. Small\" challenge, comparing objects. I also plan a bird placement game, along with a script letter-tracing game for Ol Chiki \'\341\261\232\' and Warang Chiti \'\360\221\242\271\'. A \"Fun Picture Quiz\" will conclude these activities.\n\n\n**Organizing Lesson Content**\n\nI\'m now cataloging lesson content by class and subject. I\'m starting with Class 1\'s \"Sunshine\" English, listing chapters like \"A Happy Child\" and \"Three Little Pigs.\" I\'m then organizing Class 2 and 3 Maths and Hindi lessons, meticulously adding chapter titles in Hindi (\"\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202\", \"\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262\"). This involves sorting each chapter including the one in EVS (\"\340\244\206\340\244\270-\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\270\"), detailing chapter names such as \"\340\244\212\340\244\201\340\244\237 \340\244\232\340\244\262\340\244\276\" and \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\245\202 \340\244\250\340\245\207 \340\244\226\340\245\207\340\244\262\340\245\200 \340\244\253\340\245\201\340\244\237\340\244\254\340\245\211\340\244\262.\"\n\n\n**Developing Game Features**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive game development for enhanced engagement. I\'m building a reusable game engine that supports all languages. This includes DragDropGame for comparisons, MatchGame for matching pictures with native script words and sounds, and CountGame to tally Jharkhand forest animals and fruits. I\'m also planning to incorporate more Class 5 lessons from \"\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202\" and \"\340\244\206\340\244\270-\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\270\" into a few interactive games.\n\n\n**Adding Interactive Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating new interactive components to the experience. I\'m developing a `TracingGame` for tribal alphabets, alongside a `QuizGame` with visual multiple choice and instant audio-visual feedback.\n\nI\'m also designing an animated mascot character, \"Chotu,\" a friendly deer/tribal boy, to serve as a guide. This includes animated elements like blinking, waving, and speaking, along with a cartoon world UI with tribal huts and animated animals.\nI\'m integrating features like a high contrast toggle, sound toggles, and a reward sticker book with Jharkhand-themed stickers to improve the user experience. I\'m now implementing a chatbot, \"Chotu,\" who knows the active lesson, and will interact in tribal languages, Hindi, or English.\n\n\n**Structuring Teacher/Admin Portal**\n\nI\'m now outlining the Teacher/Admin Portal, aiming for a streamlined review process. It\'ll feature one-click access to Teacher Mode, a language review queue (filterable by language), and tools to approve, reject, or edit translations. I plan audio simulation integration, chapter management tools, and an analytics dashboard to track engagement and pinpoint common mistakes.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_82659"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export type LanguageId = \'santali\' | \'ho\' | \'mundari\' | \'kurukh\' | \'khortha\';\\n\\nexport type ScriptMode = \'olchiki\' | \'warangchiti\' | \'devanagari\' | \'roman\' | \'mundaribani\';\\n\\nexport type BridgeMode = \'mother-tongue\' | \'hindi\' | \'english\' | \'bilingual\';\\n\\nexport type ReviewStatus = \'approved\' | \'teacher-reviewed\' | \'ai-draft\';\\n\\nexport interface LanguageConfig {\\n  id: LanguageId;\\n  name: string;\\n  nativeName: string;\\n  alternateNative?: string;\\n  scriptName: string;\\n  fontClass: string;\\n  scriptsAvailable: ScriptMode[];\\n  defaultScript: ScriptMode;\\n  greetingText: string;\\n  greetingTransliteration: string;\\n  audioGreetingPhonetic: string;\\n  themeColor: string;\\n  bgColor: string;\\n  iconEmoji: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  status: \'active\' | \'preview\';\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ChapterTranslation {\\n  title: string;\\n  scriptText: string;\\n  transliteration: string; // Roman or Devanagari transliteration\\n  alternateTransliteration?: string; // For Ho: Devanagari transliteration\\n  audioFile?: string;\\n  audioNarrationText?: string;\\n  videoLink?: string;\\n  reviewStatus: ReviewStatus;\\n  lastReviewedBy?: string;\\n  reviewNotes?: string;\\n  lessonSlides: LessonSlide[];\\n  gameData?: ChapterGameData;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface LessonSlide {\\n  id: string;\\n  conceptKey: string;\\n  native: string;\\n  transliteration: string;\\n  alternateTransliteration?: string;\\n  hindi: string;\\n  english: string;\\n  audioPhonetic: string;\\n  sceneType: \'inside_outside\' | \'big_small\' | \'top_bottom\' | \'near_far\' | \'rolling_sliding\' | \'general\';\\n  visualHint: string;\\n  keywords: Array<{\\n    native: string;\\n    transliteration: string;\\n    hindi: string;\\n    english: string;\\n  }>;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface DragItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: {\\n    native: string;\\n    transliteration: string;\\n    hindi: string;\\n    english: string;\\n  };\\n  emoji: string;\\n  correctZone: \'inside\' | \'outside\' | \'big\' | \'small\' | \'top\' | \'bottom\' | \'rolling\' | \'sliding\';\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ChapterGameData {\\n  dragDrop?: {\\n    instruction: {\\n      native: string;\\n      transliteration: string;\\n      hindi: string;\\n      english: string;\\n    };\\n    zones: Array<{\\n      id: string;\\n      label: {\\n        native: string;\\n        transliteration: string;\\n        hindi: string;\\n        english: string;\\n      };\\n      color: string;\\n    }>;\\n    items: DragItem[];\\n  };\\n  matching?: {\\n    instruction: {\\n      native: string;\\n      transliteration: string;\\n      hindi: string;\\n      english: string;\\n    };\\n    pairs: Array<{\\n      id: string;\\n      emoji: string;\\n      nativeWord: string;\\n      transliteration: string;\\n      hindiWord: string;\\n    }>;\\n  };\\n  counting?: {\\n    instruction: {\\n      native: string;\\n      transliteration: string;\\n      hindi: string;\\n      english: string;\\n    };\\n    items: Array<{\\n      id: string;\\n      emoji: string;\\n      name: string;\\n      count: number;\\n    }>;\\n  };\\n  tracing?: {\\n    letter: string;\\n    letterName: string;\\n    script: ScriptMode;\\n    sound: string;\\n    strokeGuide: string;\\n  };\\n  quiz?: Array<{\\n    id: string;\\n    question: {\\n      native: string;\\n      transliteration: string;\\n      hindi: string;\\n      english: string;\\n    };\\n    options: Array<{\\n      id: string;\\n      text: string;\\n      emoji?: string;\\n      isCorrect: boolean;\\n    }>;\\n    explanation: string;\\n  }>;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Chapter {\\n  id: string;\\n  chapterNumber: number;\\n  classNumber: number; // 1 to 5\\n  subjectId: \'maths\' | \'hindi\' | \'evs\' | \'english\';\\n  bookName: string;\\n  originalTitleHindi: string;\\n  originalTitleEnglish: string;\\n  coverEmoji: string;\\n  languages: {\\n    santali: ChapterTranslation;\\n    ho: ChapterTranslation;\\n    mundari: ChapterTranslation;\\n    [key: string]: ChapterTranslation;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport interface UserProgress {\\n  selectedLanguage: LanguageId;\\n  activeScript: ScriptMode;\\n  selectedClass: number;\\n  starsEarned: number;\\n  completedChapters: string[]; // chapter ids\\n  unlockedStickers: string[]; // sticker ids\\n  soundEnabled: boolean;\\n  highContrast: boolean;\\n  reduceMotion: boolean;\\n  speechRate: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface TranslationFeedback {\\n  id: string;\\n  chapterId: string;\\n  chapterTitle: string;\\n  language: LanguageId;\\n  problemType: \'spelling\' | \'wrong_word\' | \'script_display\' | \'audio_missing\' | \'other\';\\n  suggestedCorrection: string;\\n  reporterRole: \'student\' | \'teacher\' | \'parent\';\\n  timestamp: string;\\n  status: \'pending\' | \'resolved\';\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Sticker {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  nativeNames: Record<LanguageId, string>;\\n  category: \'animals\' | \'nature\' | \'tribal_culture\' | \'stars\';\\n  emoji: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  unlockedAtStars: number;\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Define TypeScript interfaces for multilingual curriculum, games, and state\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/index.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating types/index.ts\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create TypeScript types\"}"
