  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Curriculum Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/data/curriculum.ts` to integrate JCERT textbooks. I\'ve begun verifying subjects, specifically focusing on `maths`. The textbook for Class 1 will be \"\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202 (JCERT)\". Next, I plan to move on to other classes and subjects.\n\n\n**Outlining Math Curriculum Chapters**\n\nI\'ve outlined Class 1\'s chapters in detail. Chapter 1, \"\340\244\206\340\244\225\340\245\203\340\244\244\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\201 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\245\340\244\276\340\244\250,\" is complete and serves as an end-to-end benchmark. Now, I\'m setting the groundwork for the chapters that follow, including those on addition, subtraction, and numbers up to fifty. Next, I\'ll shift gears and document details for Class 2\'s curriculum, starting with \"\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202 - \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\227 2 (JCERT)\" and its first chapter.\n\n\n**Documenting Class 2 Chapters**\n\nI\'ve made headway on Class 2, meticulously documenting each chapter: \"\340\244\227\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\213 \340\244\256\340\244\227\340\244\260 \340\244\270\340\244\256\340\245\202\340\244\271\340\245\213\340\244\202 \340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\202\", \"\340\244\244\340\245\201\340\244\256 \340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\244\340\244\250\340\244\276 \340\244\265\340\244\234\340\244\274\340\244\250 \340\244\211\340\244\240\340\244\276 \340\244\270\340\244\225\340\244\244\340\245\207 \340\244\271\340\245\213?\", \"\340\244\246\340\244\270-\340\244\246\340\244\270 \340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\202 \340\244\227\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\245\213\", \"\340\244\252\340\245\210\340\244\237\340\244\260\340\245\215\340\244\250\", \"\340\244\252\340\245\210\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\202 \340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\266\340\244\276\340\244\250\", \"\340\244\234\340\244\227 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\256\340\244\227\", \"\340\244\225\340\244\260\340\245\213 \340\244\256\340\244\234\340\244\274\340\245\207 10 \340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\270\340\244\276\340\244\245\", \"\340\244\256\340\244\234\340\244\274\340\245\207\340\244\246\340\244\276\340\244\260 \340\244\246\340\244\277\340\244\250\", and \"\340\244\205\340\244\202\340\244\225 \340\244\234\340\245\213\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\245\213\". Following that, I\'m now transitioning to Class 3, beginning with the textbook \"\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202 - \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\227 3 (JCERT)\". Chapter 1, \"\340\244\225\340\244\271\340\244\276\340\244\201 \340\244\270\340\245\207 \340\244\246\340\245\207\340\244\226\340\244\276?\", is ready. I\'m moving on to outlining \"\340\244\270\340\244\202\340\244\226\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\223\340\244\202 \340\244\225\340\245\200 \340\244\211\340\244\233\340\244\262\340\244\225\340\245\202\340\244\246,\" the second chapter.\n\n\n**Cataloging Class 3 Chapters**\n\nI\'m making strong progress; I\'ve documented Class 3\'s remaining chapters, including \"\340\244\262\340\245\207\340\244\250\340\245\207 \340\244\246\340\245\207\340\244\250\340\245\207 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\226\340\245\207\340\244\262,\" \"\340\244\270\340\244\256\340\244\257-\340\244\270\340\244\256\340\244\257 \340\244\225\340\245\200 \340\244\254\340\244\276\340\244\244,\" and \"\340\244\225\340\245\214\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\270\340\244\270\340\245\207 \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200?\" Next, I\'m documenting Class 4 with its textbook \"\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202 - \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\227 4 (JCERT),\" now that I have completed Class 3. I\'ve begun to catalogue each chapter, starting with \"\340\244\210\340\244\202\340\244\237\340\245\213\340\244\202 \340\244\270\340\245\207 \340\244\254\340\244\250\340\245\200 \340\244\207\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\244.\"\n\n\n**Detailing Class 4 Chapters**\n\nI\'ve documented Class 4\'s curriculum extensively. I\'ve finished charting chapters for Class 4\'s textbook and am now progressing toward Class 5. I\'ve documented chapters from \"\340\244\206\340\244\225\340\245\203\340\244\244\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\201 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\225\340\245\213\340\244\243\" to \"\340\244\250\340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\266\340\244\276\" for mathematics and also begun work on the Hindi textbook. I have completed the initial chapters of \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\227 1\" up to \"\340\244\252\340\244\244\340\245\215\340\244\244\340\245\207 \340\244\271\340\245\200 \340\244\252\340\244\244\340\245\215\340\244\244\340\245\207\".\n\n\n**Mapping Hindi Chapters**\n\nI\'m now focusing on Hindi chapters. I\'ve documented chapters from \"\340\244\252\340\244\225\340\245\214\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\245\200\" to \"\340\244\244\340\244\277\340\244\244\340\244\262\340\245\200 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\225\340\244\262\340\245\200\" from Class 2. Currently, I\'m cataloging Class 3 chapters, starting with \"\340\244\260\340\245\207\340\244\262\340\244\227\340\244\276\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\245\200\". The goal is to fully document chapters within \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\227 3\" after this, and I\'ll continue to build a structured curriculum outline.\n\n\n**Cataloging Class 4\'s Hindi**\n\nI\'ve documented Class 3\'s Hindi, completing chapters from \"\340\244\260\340\245\207\340\244\262\340\244\227\340\244\276\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\245\200\" through to the end of the book. Now, I\'m fully cataloging Class 4\'s Hindi chapters, moving sequentially through \"\340\244\225\340\245\213\340\244\257\340\244\262\", \"\340\244\254\340\244\271\340\245\201\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\245\200 \340\244\265\340\244\277\340\244\246\340\245\215\340\244\265\340\244\276\340\244\250\" and more, from the \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\227 4\" textbook. I intend to thoroughly outline all of its chapters.\n\n\n**Charting Class 5 Chapters**\n\nI\'ve documented Class 4\'s Hindi, and now I\'m detailing Class 5\'s chapters from \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\227 5.\" I\'ve begun outlining the curriculum, starting with \"\340\244\271\340\244\256 \340\244\270\340\244\254 \340\244\270\340\245\201\340\244\256\340\244\250 \340\244\217\340\244\225 \340\244\211\340\244\252\340\244\265\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\245\207\" and progressing sequentially through \"\340\244\225\340\244\276\340\244\254\340\245\201\340\244\262\340\245\200\340\244\265\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\244\276,\" encompassing all of the chapters listed to ensure complete documentation.\n\n\n**Outlining English Curricula**\n\nI\'m now detailing the English curriculum. I have started cataloging chapters from Class 1\'s textbook, \"Sunrise - 1 (JCERT)\", including \"Myself\" and \"My Daily Routine\". I\'m steadily moving through each class, aiming to comprehensively document all chapters in \"Sunrise\" and \"Sunshine\" series. Currently, I\'m documenting Class 5, progressing sequentially through the chapters.\n\n\n**Documenting EVS Chapters**\n\nI\'m now detailing the EVS curriculum, starting with \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\252\340\244\260\340\244\277\340\244\265\340\245\207\340\244\266 - 3 (JCERT \340\244\206\340\244\270-\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\270).\" I\'ve cataloged chapters for Class 3, beginning with \"\340\244\252\340\245\202\340\244\250\340\244\256 \340\244\225\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\244\277\340\244\250\340\244\232\340\244\260\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\" and moving through the book. Then, I am proceeding with the Class 4 textbook, starting with \"\340\244\232\340\244\262\340\245\213 \340\244\232\340\244\262\340\245\207\340\244\202 \340\244\270\340\245\215\340\244\225\340\245\202\340\244\262\", and documenting each chapter diligently.\n\n\n**Cataloging EVS Chapters**\n\nI\'ve documented Class 4\'s EVS chapters, from \"\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\250\340\245\200 \340\244\225\340\245\200 \340\244\225\340\244\271\340\244\276\340\244\250\340\245\200\" to \"\340\244\254\340\244\246\340\244\262\340\244\244\340\245\207 \340\244\252\340\244\260\340\244\277\340\244\265\340\244\276\340\244\260.\" Now, I\'m documenting Class 5\'s textbook, \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\252\340\244\260\340\244\277\340\244\265\340\245\207\340\244\266 - 5 (JCERT \340\244\206\340\244\270-\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\270).\" I\'m detailing each chapter, including \"\340\244\270\340\245\201\340\244\252\340\244\260 \340\244\270\340\245\207\340\244\202\340\244\270\340\245\207\340\244\234,\" \"\340\244\270\340\244\276\340\244\201\340\244\252 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\270\340\244\252\340\245\207\340\244\260\340\244\276,\" \"\340\244\232\340\244\226\340\244\250\340\245\207 \340\244\270\340\245\207 \340\244\252\340\244\232\340\244\250\340\245\207 \340\244\244\340\244\225\" and more. My focus remains on complete, chapter-by-chapter documentation.\n\n\n**Designing Curriculum Manager**\n\nI\'m now outlining a \"Curriculum & Data Manager\" tool for the Teacher Portal. This tool will allow educators to upload chapter data as JSON, validate it, and import it into the application. It will also support custom chapter creation and editing, enhancing the overall curriculum management capability. I intend to build this out after fully documenting the chapters.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_61216"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { Chapter, LanguageId, ReviewStatus } from \'../types\';\\n\\nexport interface CurriculumValidationResult {\\n  valid: boolean;\\n  importedCount: number;\\n  errors: string[];\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Validates and normalizes user-supplied curriculum JSON data.\\n * Ensures official JCERT structure is preserved and missing language fields have safe fallbacks.\\n */\\nexport function validateAndParseCurriculumJson(jsonString: string): {\\n  result: CurriculumValidationResult;\\n  chapters: Chapter[];\\n} {\\n  const errors: string[] = [];\\n\\n  let parsed: unknown;\\n  try {\\n    parsed = JSON.parse(jsonString);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    return {\\n      result: {\\n        valid: false,\\n        importedCount: 0,\\n        errors: [`Invalid JSON format: ${(err as Error).message}`],\\n      },\\n      chapters: [],\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const rawList = Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : [parsed];\\n  const validatedChapters: Chapter[] = [];\\n\\n  rawList.forEach((item, index) => {\\n    if (!item || typeof item !== \'object\') {\\n      errors.push(`Item ${index + 1} is not a valid object.`);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const rec = item as Record<string, unknown>;\\n\\n    // Required core fields\\n    const classNumber = Number(rec.classNumber || rec.class);\\n    if (!classNumber || classNumber < 1 || classNumber > 5) {\\n      errors.push(`Item ${index + 1}: class must be a number between 1 and 5.`);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const subjectId = String(rec.subjectId || rec.subject || \'\').toLowerCase();\\n    if (![\'maths\', \'hindi\', \'evs\', \'english\'].includes(subjectId)) {\\n      errors.push(`Item ${index + 1}: subject must be one of \'maths\', \'hindi\', \'evs\', \'english\'.`);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const chapterNumber = Number(rec.chapterNumber || rec.chapter);\\n    if (!chapterNumber || chapterNumber < 1) {\\n      errors.push(`Item ${index + 1}: chapter number must be a positive integer.`);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    const originalTitleHindi = String(rec.originalTitleHindi || rec.titleHindi || rec.title || `\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\240 ${chapterNumber}`);\\n    const originalTitleEnglish = String(rec.originalTitleEnglish || rec.titleEnglish || `Chapter ${chapterNumber}`);\\n    const bookName = String(rec.bookName || rec.book || `JCERT Class ${classNumber} ${subjectId}`);\\n    const coverEmoji = String(rec.coverEmoji || \'\360\237\223\226\');\\n    const id = String(rec.id || `c${classNumber}-${subjectId}-ch${chapterNumber}`);\\n\\n    // Parse language translations\\n    const rawLangs = (rec.languages as Record<string, unknown>) || {};\\n\\n    const createSafeTranslation = (langKey: LanguageId, fallbackTitle: string) => {\\n      const l = (rawLangs[langKey] as Record<string, unknown>) || {};\\n      return {\\n        title: String(l.title || fallbackTitle),\\n        scriptText: String(l.scriptText || l.title || fallbackTitle),\\n        transliteration: String(l.transliteration || originalTitleEnglish),\\n        alternateTransliteration: l.alternateTransliteration ? String(l.alternateTransliteration) : undefined,\\n        audioFile: l.audioFile ? String(l.audioFile) : undefined,\\n        audioNarrationText: l.audioNarrationText ? String(l.audioNarrationText) : undefined,\\n        videoLink: l.videoLink ? String(l.videoLink) : undefined,\\n        reviewStatus: ([\'approved\', \'teacher-reviewed\', \'ai-draft\'].includes(String(l.reviewStatus))\\n          ? l.reviewStatus\\n          : \'ai-draft\') as ReviewStatus,\\n        lastReviewedBy: l.lastReviewedBy ? String(l.lastReviewedBy) : undefined,\\n        reviewNotes: l.reviewNotes ? String(l.reviewNotes) : undefined,\\n        lessonSlides: Array.isArray(l.lessonSlides) ? (l.lessonSlides as any) : [],\\n        gameData: l.gameData ? (l.gameData as any) : undefined,\\n      };\\n    };\\n\\n    const chapter: Chapter = {\\n      id,\\n      chapterNumber,\\n      classNumber,\\n      subjectId: subjectId as \'maths\' | \'hindi\' | \'evs\' | \'english\',\\n      bookName,\\n      originalTitleHindi,\\n      originalTitleEnglish,\\n      coverEmoji,\\n      languages: {\\n        santali: createSafeTranslation(\'santali\', originalTitleHindi),\\n        ho: createSafeTranslation(\'ho\', originalTitleHindi),\\n        mundari: createSafeTranslation(\'mundari\', originalTitleHindi),\\n      },\\n    };\\n\\n    validatedChapters.push(chapter);\\n  });\\n\\n  return {\\n    result: {\\n      valid: errors.length === 0,\\n      importedCount: validatedChapters.length,\\n      errors,\\n    },\\n    chapters: validatedChapters,\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create curriculum JSON validator and parser for user-supplied JCERT chapters and PDFs\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/curriculumImporter.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating curriculumImporter.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create curriculum importer utility\"}"
