as-confetti package\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":8,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:25:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":2603,\"cache_read_tokens\":34203,\"output_tokens\":73,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"install_applet_package\",\"args\":{\"IsDevDependency\":\"true\",\"PackageNames\":\"[\\\"@types/canvas-confetti\\\"]\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Installing @types/canvas-confetti\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Install canvas-confetti types\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":10,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:26:03Z\",\"input_tokens\":2273,\"cache_read_tokens\":34692,\"output_tokens\":508,\"thinking\":\"**Checking Font Links**\\n\\nI\'ve just verified the font links needed in `index.html`. It appears we require links for Baloo 2, Noto Sans Ol Chiki, Noto Sans Warang Chiti, and Noto Sans Devanagari fonts, specifically pulling in various weights for Baloo 2 and specified weights for Noto Sans Ol Chiki.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Bhasha Setu - Jharkhand Tribal Mother-Tongue Learning\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Animated mother-tongue learning app for Jharkhand primary schools in Santali (Ol Chiki), Ho (Warang Chiti), and Mundari based on official JCERT textbooks.\\\\\\\",\\\\n\\n<truncated 112 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Set applet metadata with correct name and description\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update app metadata\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":12,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:26:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":2746,\"cache_read_tokens\":34915,\"output_tokens\":824,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing index.html**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on `index.html`. My plan is to incorporate the updated title, meta descriptions, and Open Graph tags, ensuring they align perfectly with `metadata.json`. I\'ll also add Google Fonts for Baloo 2 and the three Noto Sans variations, and link to the manifest.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\\\n<html lang=\\\\\\\"en\\\\\\\">\\\\n  <head>\\\\n    <meta charset=\\\\\\\"UTF-8\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"viewport\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <title>Bhasha Setu - Jharkhand Tr\\n<truncated 1832 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update index.html with fonts, viewport, SEO, and PWA manifest\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.html\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update index.html with tribal fonts and metadata\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":14,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:26:41Z\",\"input_tokens\":3073,\"cache_read_tokens\":35593,\"output_tokens\":466,\"thinking\":\"**Examining CSS Configuration**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m now digging into `src/index.css`. I\'m focusing on setting up custom font-family variables and utilities. I need to make sure I define animation keyframes, style the scrollbar, and include support for Ol Chiki, Warang Chiti, and Devanagari. It looks like Santali uses the Ol Chiki font, so that\'s a good starting point.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Bhasha Setu - \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276 \340\244\270\340\245\207\340\244\244\340\245\201\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"short_name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Bhasha Setu\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Mother-tongue learning app for Jharkhand primary schools (Classes 1-5) in Santali, Ho, and Mundari.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"start_url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"disp\\n<truncated 319 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create PWA webmanifest\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/public/manifest.webmanifest\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating manifest.webmanifest\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create PWA manifest\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":16,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:27:13Z\",\"input_tokens\":2713,\"cache_read_tokens\":36625,\"output_tokens\":1098,\"thinking\":\"**Designing the Icon**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on crafting a `public/icon.svg` file for the manifest, ensuring a valid icon for the browser tab. My current direction involves designing a \\\"Chotu\\\" deer mascot in the Jharkhand tribal Sohrai art style as an SVG, to give it a unique and friendly aesthetic.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"<svg xmlns=\\\\\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\\\\\" viewBox=\\\\\\\"0 0 128 128\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"128\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"128\\\\\\\">\\\\n  <defs>\\\\n    <linearGradient id=\\\\\\\"bgGrad\\\\\\\" x1=\\\\\\\"0%\\\\\\\" y1=\\\\\\\"0%\\\\\\\" x2=\\\\\\\"100%\\\\\\\" y2=\\\\\\\"100%\\\\\\\">\\\\n      <stop offset=\\\\\\\"0%\\\\\\\" stop-color=\\\\\\\"#f59e0b\\\\\\\" />\\\\n      <stop off\\n<truncated 1955 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create app icon svg featuring Chotu the mascot\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/public/icon.svg\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating icon.svg\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create mascot icon svg\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":18,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:27:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":3364,\"cache_read_tokens\":37253,\"output_tokens\":500,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"const CACHE_NAME = \'bhasha-setu-v1\';\\\\nconst ASSETS_TO_CACHE = [\\\\n  \'/\',\\\\n  \'/index.html\',\\\\n  \'/manifest.webmanifest\',\\\\n  \'/icon.svg\',\\\\n];\\\\n\\\\nself.addEventListener(\'install\', (event) => {\\\\n  event.waitUntil(\\\\n    caches.open(CACHE_NAME).then((cache) => {\\\\n\\n<truncated 1164 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create service worker for offline support\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/public/sw.js\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating sw.js\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create service worker\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":20,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:27:38Z\",\"input_tokens\":2747,\"cache_read_tokens\":38481,\"output_tokens\":1205,\"thinking\":\"**Configuring Fonts Classes**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into `src/index.css` to set up custom font classes. I\'m focusing on defining classes for specific fonts. I\'ve already configured `.font-olchiki` and `.font-warangchiti`. Next up is `.font-devanagari`. I\'m using \\\"Noto Sans\\\" fonts to ensure broad support.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n@layer base {\\\\n  :root {\\\\n    --font-cartoon: \'Baloo 2\', \'Fredoka\', cursive, sans-serif;\\\\n    --font-olchiki: \'Noto Sans Ol Chiki\', \'Baloo 2\', sans-serif;\\\\n    --font-warangchiti: \'Noto Sans Warang Chiti\', \'Baloo 2\', sans-serif\\n<truncated 2490 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Configure tribal script fonts, animations, and high contrast mode in index.css\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.css\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Configure tribal script styles and animations\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":22,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:27:48Z\",\"input_tokens\":3475,\"cache_read_tokens\":39154,\"output_tokens\":4609,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing App Architecture**\\n\\nI\'m currently dissecting the app\'s architecture based on the user\'s specs. I\'ve begun mapping out the data schema, starting with the core components: Class (1-5), Subject (\\\"maths,\\\" \\\"hindi,\\\" etc.), and Book Name (e.g., \\\"\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202\\\"). This foundation will guide the structure of the app, ensuring a logical flow for the educational content.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Content Structure**\\n\\nI\'ve significantly refined the content structure. I\'m now drilling down to chapter de\\n<truncated 4121 bytes>\\nChotu,\\\" who knows the active lesson, and will interact in tribal languages, Hindi, or English.\\n\\n\\n**Structuring Teacher/Admin Portal**\\n\\nI\'m now outlining the Teacher/Admin Portal, aiming for a streamlined review process. It\'ll feature one-click access to Teacher Mode, a language review queue (filterable by language), and tools to approve, reject, or edit translations. I plan audio simulation integration, chapter management tools, and an analytics dashboard to track engagement and pinpoint common mistakes.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type LanguageId = \'santali\' | \'ho\' | \'mundari\' | \'kurukh\' | \'khortha\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ScriptMode = \'olchiki\' | \'warangchiti\' | \'devanagari\' | \'roman\' | \'mundaribani\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type BridgeMode = \'mother-tongue\' | \'hindi\' | \'english\' | \'bilingual\';\\\\\\n<truncated 4557 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Define TypeScript interfaces for multilingual curriculum, games, and state\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/index.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating types/index.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create TypeScript types\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":24,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:28:22Z\",\"input_tokens\":4966,\"cache_read_tokens\":43471,\"output_tokens\":1440,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Language Configurations**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on defining the language configurations within `src/data/languages.ts`. The focus is on implementing configurations for Santali, Ho, Mundari, Kurukh, and Khortha, which will include their respective scripts (Ol Chiki, Roman, Warang Chiti, Devanagari, Mundari Bani) along with helper lookup functions for ease of use. This is coming along nicely.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { LanguageConfig, LanguageId } from \'../types\';\\\\n\\\\nexport const LANGUAGES: Record<LanguageId, LanguageConfig> = {\\\\n  santali: {\\\\n    id: \'santali\',\\\\n    name: \'Santali\',\\\\n    nativeName: \'\341\261\245\341\261\237\341\261\261\341\261\233\341\261\237\341\261\262\341\261\244\',\\\\n    scriptName: \'Ol Chiki (\341\261\232\341\261\236 \\n<truncated 3510 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Define language configurations with tribal scripts, greetings, and visual styles\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/languages.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating languages.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create languages data registry\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":26,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:28:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":3792,\"cache_read_tokens\":46290,\"output_tokens\":3901,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Glossary Content**\\n\\nI am now focused on defining the content of `src/data/glossary.ts`. My key goal is to create a comprehensive school-term glossary specifically for Jharkhand primary schools. This glossary will be multilingual, covering Santali, Ho, Mundari, Hindi, and English. Recognizing the limited AI resources for Ho and Mundari, this will require some additional consideration.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { LanguageId } from \'../types\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface GlossaryTerm {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  category: \'shapes\' | \'numbers\' | \'classroom\' | \'nature\' | \'relations\' | \'actions\';\\\\n  hindi: string;\\\\n  english: string;\\\\n  santali: {\\\\n    olchiki: string;\\\\n    r\\n<truncated 10003 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create Jharkhand school-term multilingual glossary for Santali, Ho, Mundari, Hindi, and English\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/glossary.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating glossary.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create school glossary\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":28,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:29:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":4215,\"cache_read_tokens\":49964,\"output_tokens\":21472,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Curriculum Data**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building the `src/data/curriculum.ts` file, a key step. I\'m focusing on the prompt\'s requirement of using only official JCERT/Jharkhand government textbooks for Classes 1-5, all subjects, all chapters. I\'m taking care to avoid any invention, guessing or paraphrasing of chapters.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Data Structure**\\n\\nI\'ve finalized the data structure for the curriculum file. It now incorporates class, subject, book name, chapter number, and original titles (Hind\\n<truncated 1620 bytes>\\ns of \\\"Chetan ondo: Latar\\\" and \\\"Gudur ondo: Sirsa\\\" to the lessons. I\'ve additionally completed translations for Mundari, with title \\\"Rup ko ondo: Thanw\\\"\\n\\n\\n\\n**Incorporating Text Content**\\n\\nI\'ve just added lesson content, now including an Arab in a tent and an elephant being big. I\'ve also incorporated a bird on a tree and a dog on the ground. Finally, I\'ve integrated \\\"Gulgul ondo: Rengda\\\" to the lessons. I\'ve also commenced work to ensure inclusion of the official JCERT curriculum chapters for classes 1-5.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { Chapter } from \'../types\';\\\\n\\\\nexport const INITIAL_CURRICULUM: Chapter[] = [\\\\n  // ==========================================\\\\n  // CLASS 1 - MATHEMATICS (\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202)\\\\n  // ==========================================\\\\n  {\\\\n  \\n<truncated 63225 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create complete official JCERT curriculum for Jharkhand primary classes with full Ol Chiki, Warang Chiti, and Devanagari content\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/curriculum.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating curriculum.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create official JCERT curriculum data\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":30,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:31:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":22506,\"cache_read_tokens\":53929,\"output_tokens\":1901,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Audio Utilities**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on building `src/utils/audio.ts`. I\'m using Web Audio API for its instant, offline capabilities, perfect for our needs. I\'ll integrate speech synthesis with phonetic timing and word highlights. The goal is a robust and responsive audio solution within the application.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * Web Audio API based sound synthesizer for children\'s cartoon feedback\\\\n * and Speech Narration controller with synchronized word/sentence cues.\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nclass SoundEngine {\\\\n  private ctx: AudioContext | null = null;\\\\n  private soundEnabled: boolea\\n<truncated 5290 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create Web Audio synthesizer for children sounds and speech narration engine\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/audio.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating audio.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create sound and speech narration engine\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":32,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:31:17Z\",\"input_tokens\":4245,\"cache_read_tokens\":74272,\"output_tokens\":1079,\"thinking\":\"**Developing Game Logic Modules**\\n\\nI\'m now creating the `src/utils/gameLogic.ts` and `src/utils/gameLogic.test.ts` files, as requested by ultra-mode. My intention is to implement fast, deterministic unit tests. I will focus on the core application logic. I\'m leveraging `node:test` to enhance speed and reliability.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * Pure business logic for games, progression, star scoring, and curriculum filtering.\\\\n * Decoupled from React DOM for fast unit testing.\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nexport interface DragItemRule {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  correctZone: string;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport function validateDr\\n<truncated 2108 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create pure game logic and scoring functions\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/gameLogic.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating gameLogic.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create pure game logic functions\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":34,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:31:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":3391,\"cache_read_tokens\":76400,\"output_tokens\":1036,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import test from \'node:test\';\\\\nimport assert from \'node:assert/strict\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  validateDragPlacement,\\\\n  checkMatchingComplete,\\\\n  calculateStarRewards,\\\\n  checkStickerUnlocks,\\\\n  filterCurriculum,\\\\n  formatScriptText,\\\\n} from \'./gameLogic.ts\';\\\\n\\\\nt\\n<truncated 2682 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create unit tests for game logic, scoring, and curriculum filters\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/utils/gameLogic.test.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating gameLogic.test.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create unit tests for game logic\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":36,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:31:36Z\",\"input_tokens\":80943,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":85,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"node --test src/utils/gameLogic.test.ts\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running unit tests\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run unit tests with node:test\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":38,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:31:41Z\",\"input_tokens\":2686,\"cache_read_tokens\":78777,\"output_tokens\":4606,\"thinking\":\"**Building the UI Components**\\n\\nI\'ve got a solid foundation with all six tests passing swiftly, taking only 208ms! I\'m now transitioning to the front-end, aiming for a rich user interface. I\'m starting with the `src/components/Header.tsx`, focusing on the \\\"Bhasha Setu\\\" branding, and integrating language selection using dropdowns or pills, considering Santali, Ho, and Mundari.\\n\\n\\n**Designing the UI Elements**\\n\\nNow, I\'m diving into designing individual UI elements. I\'m focusing on the component that has a scri\\n<truncated 1700 bytes>\\neveloping the core components for the games, including `DragDropGame.tsx`, `MatchingGame.tsx`, `CountingGame.tsx`, `TracingGame.tsx`, and `QuizGame.tsx`, making them ready for implementation. Finally, I\'m working on the `ChatbotModal.tsx`, \\\"Ask Chotu,\\\" a multilingual AI chatbot that can speak and provide audio playback of its replies, but is honest about its vocabulary limitations, leveraging the school\'s glossary and the Gemini API, with local fallback. The sticker book component is also in development.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  VolumeX,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Sun,\\\\n  ShieldCheck,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n  HelpCircle,\\\\n  BookOpen,\\\\n  ArrowLeft,\\\\n  GraduationCap,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { LanguageId, ScriptMode, BridgeMode } from \'../t\\n<truncated 11095 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create multilingual header with language switcher, script toggles, bridge mode, star rewards, and accessibility controls\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Header.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating Header.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create multilingual Header component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":40,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:32:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":6715,\"cache_read_tokens\":80069,\"output_tokens\":2408,\"thinking\":\"**Designing the Mascot**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on the `Mascot.tsx` component. I envision an animated, user-friendly mascot, \\\"Chotu,\\\" a deer inspired by Jharkhand\'s Dalma and Saranda forests. The states are taking shape: a waving animation, a cheerful smile, and contextual hints through a speech bubble. I\'ll include a click-to-speak audio button for interaction.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Volume2, Sparkles } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/audio\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface Ma