\":2924,\"cache_read_tokens\":89337,\"output_tokens\":1423,\"thinking\":\"**Designing Class Selection**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on designing the \\\"Choose class\\\" component, specifically the visual representation of classes 1 and 2. The goal is animal-themed, big, colourful buttons. I\'ve chosen an elephant for class 1 and a deer for class 2. I\'m thinking about the visual appeal and user experience for the button designs, and how they contribute to the overall flow.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Volume2, Sparkles, ChevronRight } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { CLASSES } from \'../data/curriculum\';\\\\nimport { LanguageId } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { LANGUAGES } from \'../data/languages\';\\\\nimport { Mascot } from \'./M\\n<truncated 4056 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create ClassSelector component with 5 animal-themed buttons and audio cues\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ClassSelector.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ClassSelector.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create ClassSelector component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":46,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:33:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":3758,\"cache_read_tokens\":90128,\"output_tokens\":1270,\"thinking\":\"**Designing Subject Selection**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on the component for subject selection, specifically `SubjectSelector.tsx`. The user flow dictates large icon tiles with sound feedback on tap. I\'m considering the subjects: Mathematics (\340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 \340\244\225\340\244\276 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\246\340\245\202 / \341\261\256\341\261\236\341\261\240\341\261\267\341\261\237 / Math) and Language Hindi (\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 / \341\261\257\341\261\237\341\261\271\341\261\250\341\261\245\341\261\244) as potential options for the component.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { ChevronRight, Sparkles } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { SUBJECTS } from \'../data/curriculum\';\\\\nimport { LanguageId } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/audio\';\\\\nimport { Mascot } from \'./Mascot\';\\\\n\\\\ninte\\n<truncated 3502 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create SubjectSelector component with large touch tiles and JCERT book labels\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/SubjectSelector.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating SubjectSelector.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create SubjectSelector component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":48,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:33:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":3599,\"cache_read_tokens\":91756,\"output_tokens\":2252,\"thinking\":\"**Designing Chapter Map**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on the ChapterMap component now. I\'m visualizing a cartoon landscape with a winding path and numbered chapter cards as stepping stones. Completed chapters will be highlighted with stars. This design reflects the user flow\'s \\\"Choose chapter\\\" step, emphasizing a visual, interactive experience.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Star, CheckCircle2, Play, Sparkles, BookCheck, ShieldAlert } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { Chapter, LanguageId, ScriptMode } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/audio\';\\\\nimport { Mascot } from \'./Mascot\'\\n<truncated 7540 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create visual ChapterMap learning trail with JCERT titles, review badges, and progress indicators\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ChapterMap.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ChapterMap.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create ChapterMap component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":50,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:33:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":2482,\"cache_read_tokens\":95305,\"output_tokens\":4905,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Visual Explanation**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on building the `StoryAnimation.tsx` component. The aim is to create animated, illustrated explanations using cartoon scenes, moving characters, and visuals that bring each concept to life. This interactive element will be key to enhancing user engagement.\\n\\n\\n**Visualizing Spatial Relationships**\\n\\nI\'m currently designing interactive visuals for concepts like \\\"inside/outside,\\\" \\\"big/small,\\\" and \\\"top/bottom.\\\" I envision a desert scene with a tent and camel, an animated forest with an elephant and puppy, and a Sal tree with a bird and monkey. The goal is to animate these elements based on user interaction to clearly show the relationship with the labels.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Play, RotateCcw, Volume2, Sparkles } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/audio\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface StoryAnimationProps {\\\\n  sceneType: \'inside_outside\' | \'big_small\' | \'top_bottom\' | \'near_fa\\n<truncated 16984 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create interactive animated cartoon world scenes for inside/outside, big/small, top/bottom, and rolling/sliding concepts\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/StoryAnimation.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating StoryAnimation.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create StoryAnimation cartoon component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":52,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:34:03Z\",\"input_tokens\":5248,\"cache_read_tokens\":97702,\"output_tokens\":2787,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Interactive Games**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building interactive games! My plan involves reviewing the required game types for the chapter: drag and drop, matching, counting, quizzes, sorting, puzzles, and tracing letters. I\'m focusing on building individual, reusable game templates within the `src/components/games/` directory, starting with `DragDrop`.\\n\\n\\n**Designing Game Interactions**\\n\\nI\'ve been concentrating on the core interactions for each game type now. For drag-and-drop, I\'m ensuring smooth touch screen compatibility with visual feedback. The matching game will feature native script words and audio prompts. The counting game is planned to have large, intuitive buttons. My primary focus is on the user experience.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Sparkles, CheckCircle2, RotateCcw, Volume2 } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { DragItem } from \'../../types\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../../utils/audio\';\\\\nimport { validateDragPlacement } from \'../../utils/g\\n<truncated 8250 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create interactive Drag and Drop sorting game component\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/games/DragDropGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating DragDropGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create DragDropGame component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":54,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:34:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":24338,\"cache_read_tokens\":81667,\"output_tokens\":1950,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { CheckCircle2, RotateCcw, Volume2 } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../../utils/audio\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface MatchingGameProps {\\\\n  instruction: {\\\\n    native: string;\\\\n    transliteration: string;\\\\n \\n<truncated 6353 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create MatchingGame component for pairing pictures with tribal script words\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/games/MatchingGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating MatchingGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create MatchingGame component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":56,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:34:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":5203,\"cache_read_tokens\":102868,\"output_tokens\":1682,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Counting Game**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on building the `CountingGame.tsx` component. The game will involve counting forest deer, mangoes, and sal flowers. I plan to use large number buttons, and the numbers will be displayed in the mother tongue: Mit, Bar, Pe / Miyad, Bariya, Apiya / \340\244\217\340\244\225, \340\244\246\340\245\213, \340\244\244\340\245\200\340\244\250.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { RotateCcw, CheckCircle2 } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../../utils/audio\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface CountingGameProps {\\\\n  instruction: {\\\\n    native: string;\\\\n    transliteration: string;\\\\n    hindi:\\n<truncated 5350 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create CountingGame component for numbers in tribal languages\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/games/CountingGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating CountingGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create CountingGame component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":58,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:34:52Z\",\"input_tokens\":4023,\"cache_read_tokens\":105925,\"output_tokens\":2229,\"thinking\":\"**Developing Tracing Game**\\n\\nI\'m now building `src/components/games/TracingGame.tsx`, focusing on interactive HTML5 Canvas letter tracing. The goal is to create a game where children aged 6-11 can trace tribal script letters using touch or a mouse. Initially, I\'m implementing Ol Chiki \'\341\261\232\' (LA) and Warang Chiti \'\360\221\242\271\'.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useRef, useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { RotateCcw, CheckCircle2, Sparkles, Volume2 } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../../utils/audio\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface TracingGameProps {\\\\n  tracingData: {\\\\n    letter: string;\\\\n   \\n<truncated 6448 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create HTML5 canvas TracingGame component for Ol Chiki, Warang Chiti, and Devanagari letters\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/games/TracingGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating TracingGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create TracingGame component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":60,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:35:08Z\",\"input_tokens\":2455,\"cache_read_tokens\":109924,\"output_tokens\":1927,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport confetti from \'canvas-confetti\';\\\\nimport { CheckCircle2, XCircle, RotateCcw, Volume2, Sparkles } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../../utils/audio\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface QuizQuestion {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n\\n<truncated 6205 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create visual QuizGame component with multiple choice options and confetti celebration\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/games/QuizGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating QuizGame.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create QuizGame component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":62,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:35:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":2139,\"cache_read_tokens\":112283,\"output_tokens\":2425,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Game Hub**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on building the `GameHub.tsx` component. My goal is a unified container with tabs that will house various game types. I\'m currently envisioning tabs for Drag & Drop (both inside and outside the target), Matching (words and pictures), Counting (numbers one to five), and Letter Tracing (including Ol Chiki and Warang Chiti). I\'m considering the best tab structure for this diverse set of game types.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport confetti from \'canvas-confetti\';\\\\nimport { ArrowLeft, Sparkles, Trophy, Star, Gamepad2 } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { ChapterGameData } from \'../../types\';\\\\nimport { DragDropGame } from \'./games/DragDropG\\n<truncated 7841 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create GameHub component managing tabs between DragDrop, Matching, Counting, Tracing, and Quiz games\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/GameHub.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating GameHub.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create GameHub container component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":64,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:35:45Z\",\"input_tokens\":2655,\"cache_read_tokens\":114408,\"output_tokens\":4743,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Lesson Views**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on the components of the lesson view. I\'m visualizing the core elements: the chapter explanation with native script, transliteration, and a toggle, and the audio play button. I\'m outlining how these components will work together to create an engaging learning experience.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Play,\\\\n  Pause,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  ChevronLeft,\\\\n  ChevronRight,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Gamepad2,\\\\n  HelpCircle,\\\\n  Video,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  BookCheck,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n  BookOpen,\\\\n} f\\n<truncated 15748 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create rich LessonView component with synchronized word audio narration, interactive scenes, bridge toggles, and video storybook\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/LessonView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating LessonView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create LessonView component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":66,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:36:19Z\",\"input_tokens\":5062,\"cache_read_tokens\":116924,\"output_tokens\":5722,\"thinking\":\"**Designing \\\"Chotu\\\"**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on the chatbot component, \\\"Chotu.\\\" I envision a friendly cartoon character interacting with children. It will leverage context about the class, subject, and chapter to answer doubts in simple language, in the child\'s preferred language. This design should be accessible for children who may be beginners in the language of instruction.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \'@google/genai\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Send,\\\\n  Volume2,\\\\n  VolumeX,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Bot,\\\\n  User,\\\\n  Mic,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  ShieldCheck,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { Lang\\n<truncated 18996 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create child-safe multilingual Chatbot modal with Gemini API integration and instant offline fallback\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ChatbotModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ChatbotModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create ChatbotModal component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":68,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:36:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":6074,\"cache_read_tokens\":121826,\"output_tokens\":1579,\"thinking\":\"**Designing Sticker Book Modal**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on the sticker book modal component. I\'ve got the rewards system sketched out: stars, badges, and a sticker collection that unlocks with game progress. I\'m visualizing the visual celebration with confetti and sound after each unlock. The sticker designs are starting to take shape, focusing on Jharkhand\'s wildlife and tribal heritage.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Sparkles, Star, Lock, Award, Volume2 } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { STICKERS } from \'../data/curriculum\';\\\\nimport { LanguageId } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/audio\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface StickerBookModal\\n<truncated 5155 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create StickerBookModal celebrating Jharkhand wildlife, trees, and tribal culture stickers\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/StickerBookModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating StickerBookModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create StickerBookModal component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":70,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:37:13Z\",\"input_tokens\":3901,\"cache_read_tokens\":125772,\"output_tokens\":1842,\"thinking\":\"**Designing Report Modal**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on constructing the `ReportModal` component. My goal is to equip it with a \\\"Report wrong translation\\\" button. This button will provide a feedback mechanism, allowing users (students and teachers) to submit reports directly to the relevant language\'s review queue. The reports will cover spelling errors, missing audio, and translation inconsistencies, linked to specific chapter details.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { AlertCircle, CheckCircle2, Send } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { LanguageId, TranslationFeedback } from \'../types\';\\\\nimport { LANGUAGES } from \'../data/languages\';\\\\nimport { sound } from \'../utils/audio\';\\n<truncated 6436 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create ReportModal component for submitting translation feedback into teacher review queue\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ReportModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ReportModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create ReportModal component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":72,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:37:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":4172,\"cache_read_tokens\":127541,\"output_tokens\":5588,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Teacher Portal**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on the `TeacherPortal.tsx` component. The key features will be the teacher login, language assignment, and the review queue. I\'m imagining this queue will allow teachers to edit, approve or reject AI drafts and upload native-speaker audio, specific to their assigned languages. This sounds like it will get complex in the UI.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Teacher Portal Features**\\n\\nNow, I\'m integrating features like curriculum management. The teacher selector will include individuals like Shri Hemant Soren, Dr. Dobro Buriuli, and Shri Mangal Singh Munda. The review queue will let teachers filter by language and status, edit inline, and approve/reject drafts, also record audio. The analytics dashboard is to feature completion rates, accuracy by language, and insight into common misconceptions.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  GraduationCap,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  XCircle,\\\\n  FileEdit,\\\\n  Download,\\\\n  Upload,\\\\n  Mic,\\\\n  BarChart3,\\\\n  ListFilter,\\\\n  ArrowLeft,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  BookCheck,\\\\n  AlertCircle,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n} from \'lucide-r\\n<truncated 20511 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create TeacherPortal with review queue, inline editing, student report resolution, and AI4Bharat dataset export\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/TeacherPortal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating TeacherPortal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create TeacherPortal component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":74,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:38:03Z\",\"input_tokens\":5931,\"cache_read_tokens\":131656,\"output_tokens\":4007,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing The App Shell**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on building the application\'s core shell within `src/App.tsx`. I\'m carefully reviewing the required state flow. Currently, I\'m defining `currentLanguage` and `activeScript` with their specific types, with `currentLanguage` persisting in localStorage. These fundamental pieces will be the backbone of the application\'s interface.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Core State Elements**\\n\\nI\'m now diving deep into the application\'s core state structure. I\'ve fleshed out the state shape, incorporating new variables for `bridgeMode` with three potential string values. Additionally, I\'ve detailed the `currentScreen` options: welcome, classes, subjects, chapters, lesson, games, and teacher. I\'ve also added types for `selectedClass`, `selectedSubject`, `selectedChapter`, and several persisted variables: `starsCount`, `completedChapters`, `unlockedStickerIds`, `soundEnabled`, and `highContrast`. Finally, I\'m setting up types for various modal states and a feedback queue.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * @license\\\\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nimport React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  LanguageId,\\\\n  ScriptMode,\\\\n  BridgeMode,\\\\n  Chapter,\\\\n  ReviewStatus,\\\\n  TranslationFeedback,\\\\n} from \'./types\';\\\\nimport { L\\n<truncated 13804 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Build main App component with complete user flow, navigation, persistent state, and modal bindings\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Build main App component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":76,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:38:30Z\",\"input_tokens\":4288,\"cache_read_tokens\":137640,\"output_tokens\":1843,\"thinking\":\"**Crafting Documentation**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on the README.md file, ensuring it\'s comprehensive. I aim to detail the addition of chapters, audio, games, and language options for this project, catering specifically to your needs as an expert. This README will serve as a clear guide for all future modifications.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"# Bhasha Setu (\341\261\265\341\261\267\341\261\237\341\261\245\341\261\237 \341\261\245\341\261\256\341\261\233\341\261\251 / \360\221\242\252\360\221\243\201\360\221\243\236\360\221\243\201 \360\221\242\267\360\221\243\210\360\221\243\225\360\221\243\203 / \340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276 \340\244\270\340\245\207\340\244\244\340\245\201)\\\\n\\\\n**Bhasha Setu** is an animated, mother-tongue primary learning application built for tribal children in Jharkhand schools (Classes 1 to 5), sup\\n<truncated 5865 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create complete README with architecture, schema, teacher guide, and extensibility documentation\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/README.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating README.md\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create README documentation\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":78,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:38:45Z\",\"input_tokens\":4167,\"cache_read_tokens\":139780,\"output_tokens\":49,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet to check for build errors\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":80,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:38:49Z\",\"input_tokens\":2276,\"cache_read_tokens\":141802,\"output_tokens\":105,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"node --test src/utils/gameLogic.test.ts\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Running unit tests\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Verify unit tests pass\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":82,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:39:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":2699,\"cache_read_tokens\":141918,\"output_tokens\":206,\"thinking\":\"**Testing the Logic**\\n\\nI\'ve successfully run the unit tests; they all passed. Now, I\'m ensuring the app compiles cleanly before restarting the development server, as directed, since hot reload is off. The next step is to examine the output of the restart.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting development server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server for fresh render\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":84,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:39:06Z\",\"input_tokens\":2436,\"cache_read_tokens\":142523,\"output_tokens\":218,\"thinking\":\"**Initiating Playwright-CLI**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on integrating `playwright-cli` with `run_command` to inspect desktop and mobile renderings. I\'m focusing on user journeys and screenshot generation for visual verification. Right now, I\'m setting up a directory named `.playwright-cli` and initiating a connection to `http://localhost:3000`. Next, I\'ll run a bash command.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT\\\\nmkdir -p .playwright-cli\\\\nplaywright-cli open --browser=chromium http://localhost:3000\\\\nplaywright-cli resize 1440 900\\\\nplaywright-cli screenshot --filename=.playwright-cli/r1-welcome-desktop.png\\\\nplaywright-cli snapshot\\\\\\n<truncated 2 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"8000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Capturing desktop welcome screen\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Open app and capture welcome screen snapshot and screenshot\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":86,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:39:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":2770,\"cache_read_tokens\":144938,\"output_tokens\":62,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/.playwright-cli/r1-welcome-desktop.png\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing welcome screen screenshot\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View welcome screen screenshot\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":88,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:39:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":3433,\"cache_read_tokens\":145515,\"output_tokens\":637,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Font Rendering**\\n\\nI\'ve made a key observation from comparing Ol Chiki and Warang Chiti characters. The Ol Chiki, representing `\341\261\245\341\261\237\341\261\261\341\261\233\341\261\237\341\261\262\341\261\244`, renders perfectly. However, the Warang Chiti script, specifically `\360\221\242\271\360\221\243\211\360\221\243\200 \360\221\243\216\360\221\243\213\360\221\243\234`, displays as boxes on some headless Linux environments, suggesting a missing font or rendering issue with that specific script when the Google Font web is used.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating Font Availability**\\n\\nI\'m now digging deeper into the font loading and CSS linking. It seems the issue stems from Google Fonts not fully supporting `Noto+Sans+Warang+Chiti` in its v2 CSS. I\'m exploring Google Fonts directly to confirm its availability. Also, exploring the need for a direct `@font-face` declaration or webfont implementation for this script. I\'m also ensuring Devanagari transliteration is properly handled for Ho speakers.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s \\\\\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Sans+Warang+Chiti\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking Google Fonts for Warang Chiti\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check Noto Sans Warang Chiti availability\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":90,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:39:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":3195,\"cache_read_tokens\":149031,\"output_tokens\":217,\"thinking\":\"**Locating Missing Font**\\n\\nI\'ve hit a snag: `Noto Sans Warang Chiti` isn\'t accessible via the Google Fonts CSS API, hence the 400 error. The browser can\'t download the font for Warang Chiti. My next move is to track down the font file\'s location, see if I can procure it elsewhere, or explore SVG/web font alternatives.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s -I \\\\\\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/notofonts/noto-fonts/main/hinted/ttf/NotoSansWarangChiti/NotoSansWarangChiti-Regular.ttf\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking raw github for Noto Sans Warang Chiti ttf\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check font file on GitHub\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":92,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:39:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":2815,\"cache_read_tokens\":150146,\"output_tokens\":110,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s \\\\\\\"https://api.github.com/search/code?q=NotoSansWarangChiti-Regular.ttf\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching for font on github\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search NotoSansWarangChiti font file\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":94,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:39:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":2380,\"cache_read_tokens\":150812,\"output_tokens\":127,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s -I \\\\\\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/googlefonts/noto-fonts/main/unhinted/ttf/NotoSansWarangChiti/NotoSansWarangChiti-Regular.ttf\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking googlefonts repo for Warang Chiti\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check googlefonts/noto-fonts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":96,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":2717,\"cache_read_tokens\":151030,\"output_tokens\":84,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"search_web\",\"args\":{\"query\":\"\\\"\\\\\\\"NotoSansWarangChiti\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"github.com\\\\\\\" ttf\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Searching for Warang Chiti font link\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Search Warang Chiti font ttf link\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":98,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":3007,\"cache_read_tokens\":151575,\"output_tokens\":216,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Nomenclature Discrepancies**\\n\\nI\'ve noticed a subtle but potentially significant naming discrepancy. The font is officially called `Warang Citi`, yet the GitHub repository uses `warang-citi` with a \'C\' instead of \'Ch\'. This difference warrants further investigation, so I\'m now examining the `NotoSansWarangCiti-Regular` font file directly from the repository.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s -I \\\\\\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/notofonts/warang-citi/main/fonts/NotoSansWarangCiti/unhinted/ttf/NotoSansWarangCiti-Regular.ttf\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking NotoSansWarangCiti ttf url\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check Warang Citi TTF URL\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":100,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":2812,\"cache_read_tokens\":152501,\"output_tokens\":115,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s \\\\\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/notofonts/warang-citi/contents\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking warang-citi repo contents\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Get warang-citi repo structure\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":102,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:19Z\",\"input_tokens\":4162,\"cache_read_tokens\":155152,\"output_tokens\":117,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s \\\\\\\"https://api.github.com/repos/notofonts/warang-citi/releases/latest\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking warang-citi releases\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check warang-citi latest release\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":104,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:22Z\",\"input_tokens\":4069,\"cache_read_tokens\":157108,\"output_tokens\":281,\"thinking\":\"**Downloading the Font**\\n\\nI\'ve found the Warang Chiti font at the link provided and I am downloading the zip file right now. Once downloaded, I plan to unzip it directly into the `/public/fonts/` directory. This should ensure native, precise, and offline rendering of Warang Chiti, improving the overall display of the language.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"mkdir -p public/fonts\\\\ncurl -L -o public/fonts/warang.zip \\\\\\\"https://github.com/notofonts/warang-citi/releases/download/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002.zip\\\\\\\"\\\\nunzip -q public/fonts/warang.zip -d public/fonts/warang\\\\nfind public/fonts/wa\\n<truncated 54 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"8000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Downloading Warang Chiti font\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Download and install Warang Chiti TTF font\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":106,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:34Z\",\"input_tokens\":2650,\"cache_read_tokens\":159095,\"output_tokens\":91,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"status\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"f7a91744-aabe-438b-8fbd-f4791e9ad47b/task-105\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking font download task status\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check background download task\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":108,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:37Z\",\"input_tokens\":2360,\"cache_read_tokens\":159600,\"output_tokens\":105,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"status\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"f7a91744-aabe-438b-8fbd-f4791e9ad47b/task-105\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking font task status\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check background task status\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":110,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":2374,\"cache_read_tokens\":159815,\"output_tokens\":1287,\"content\":\"An asynchronous task has finished.\\nTask id: f7a91744-aabe-438b-8fbd-f4791e9ad47b/task-105\\nTask description: mkdir -p public/fonts\\ncurl -L -o public/fonts/warang.zip \\\"https://github.com/notofonts/warang-citi/releases/download/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002.zip\\\"\\nunzip -q public/fonts/warang.zip -d public/fonts/warang\\nfind public/fonts/warang -name \\\"*.ttf\\\"\\nrm -f public/fonts/warang.zip\\nCommand output:\\npublic/fonts/warang/NotoSansWarangCiti/unhinted/ttf/NotoSansWarangCiti-Regular.ttf\\npublic\\n<truncated 1444 bytes>\\nng/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002/NotoSansWarangCiti/googlefonts/ttf/NotoSansWarangCiti-Regular.ttf  \\n  inflating: public/fonts/warang/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002/NotoSansWarangCiti/googlefonts/ttf/NotoSansWarangCiti-Bold.ttf  \\n  inflating: public/fonts/warang/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002/OFL.txt  \\n  inflating: public/fonts/warang/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002/README.md  \\n  inflating: public/fonts/warang/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002/AUTHORS.txt  \\n  inflating: public/fonts/warang/NotoSansWarangCiti-v3.002/CONTRIBUTORS.txt  \\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"cp public/fonts/warang/NotoSansWarangCiti/googlefonts/ttf/NotoSansWarangCiti-Regular.ttf public/fonts/NotoSansWarangCiti-Regular.ttf\\\\ncp public/fonts/warang/NotoSansWarangCiti/googlefonts/ttf/NotoSansWarangCiti-Bold.ttf public/fonts/NotoSansWarangCiti-Bol\\n<truncated 58 bytes>\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\".\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Moving Warang Citi fonts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Organize Warang Citi fonts in public/fonts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":113,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:40:52Z\",\"input_tokens\":3992,\"cache_read_tokens\":159988,\"output_tokens\":736,\"thinking\":\"**Locating the Font File**\\n\\nI\'ve confirmed the font file, `NotoSansWarangCiti-Regular.ttf`, is exactly where I expected it \342\200\223 tucked neatly inside `public/fonts/`.  My next step is to configure the `@font-face` rule within `src/index.css`. This should allow me to start using both `\'Noto Sans Warang Chiti\'` and `\'Noto Sans Warang\'` in my project.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Remove invalid Google Font link and clean up font imports\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"25\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update Google Fonts link without invalid Warang Chiti parameter\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    <!-- Google Fonts for Tribal Scripts & Playful Children\'s UI -->\\\\n    <link rel=\\\\\\\"preconnect\\\\\\\" href=\\\\\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <link rel=\\\\\\\"preconnect\\\\\\\" href=\\\\\\\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\\\\\\\" crossorigin />\\\\n    <link href=\\\\\\\"https://fonts.goo\\n<truncated 214 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"15\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    <!-- Google Fonts for Tribal Scripts & Playful Children\'s UI -->\\\\n    <link rel=\\\\\\\"preconnect\\\\\\\" href=\\\\\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <link rel=\\\\\\\"preconnect\\\\\\\" href=\\\\\\\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\\\\\\\" crossorigin />\\\\n    <link href=\\\\\\\"https://fonts.goo\\n<truncated 244 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.html\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update Google Fonts link in index.html\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":115,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:41:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":165378,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1483,\"thinking\":\"**Refining Font Implementation**\\n\\nI\'m now updating `src/index.css` to incorporate the `@font-face` rule for the \'Noto Sans Warang Chiti\' font. This involves specifying the font family and source URL for proper rendering, and I\'ll ensure all relevant character sets are covered for comprehensive display.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n@font-face {\\\\n  font-family: \'Noto Sans Warang Chiti\';\\\\n  src: url(\'/fonts/NotoSansWarangCiti-Regular.ttf\') format(\'truetype\');\\\\n  font-weight: 400 700;\\\\n  font-style: normal;\\\\n  font-display: swap;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n@font-face {\\\\n  font-f\\n<truncated 2949 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add local font-face definitions for Noto Sans Warang Chiti/Citi in src/index.css\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.css\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add Warang Chiti @font-face\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":117,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:41:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":3027,\"cache_read_tokens\":164014,\"output_tokens\":1139,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Welcome Text Issues**\\n\\nI\'m currently investigating a rendering issue on the welcome screen. Specifically, I\'m examining the text on line 37 of `WelcomeScreen.tsx` for problematic characters. The Punjabi script contains the characters `\340\250\206\340\250\252\340\250\243\340\251\200 \340\250\256\340\250\276\340\250\244\340\250\255\340\250\276`, and I\'m looking into how these are being interpreted.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Improve welcome screen greeting copy and script typography\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"58\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Use exact Santali, Ho, and Mundari native scripts without missing glyphs\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex flex-col items-center justify-center my-2\\\\\\\">\\\\n          <Mascot\\\\n            speechText=\\\\\\\"\341\261\241\341\261\232\341\261\246\341\261\237\341\261\250! / \360\221\242\271\360\221\243\211\360\221\243\200 \360\221\243\216\360\221\243\213\360\221\243\234 / \340\244\234\340\245\213\340\244\271\340\244\276\340\244\260! Welcome to Bhasha Setu!\\\\\\\"\\\\n            speechTransliteration=\\\\\\\"\341\261\237\341\261\242\\n<truncated 854 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"42\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex flex-col items-center justify-center my-2\\\\\\\">\\\\n          <Mascot\\\\n            speechText=\\\\\\\"\341\261\241\341\261\232\341\261\246\341\261\237\341\261\250! / \360\221\242\271\360\221\243\211\360\221\243\200 \360\221\243\216\360\221\243\213\360\221\243\234 / \340\244\234\340\245\213\340\244\271\340\244\276\340\244\260! Welcome to Bhasha Setu!\\\\\\\"\\\\n            speechTransliteration=\\\\\\\"Which is\\n<truncated 731 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WelcomeScreen.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating WelcomeScreen.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Refine welcome subtitle with dedicated font classes\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":119,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T13:41:24Z\",\"input_tokens\":3437,\"cache_read_tokens\":164931,\"output_tokens\":98,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WelcomeScreen.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"65\",\"StartLine\":\"35\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing lines 35-65 of WelcomeScreen.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View WelcomeScreen lines\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":121,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\