  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Feedback**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s feedback, focusing on the discrepancy between their reported experience and the actual content. Specifically, I\'m trying to pinpoint where the user\'s perception of accuracy falters concerning subjects and chapters within the Jharkhand context. This analysis will guide my understanding of the problem and potential solutions.\n\n\n**Identifying Textbook Errors**\n\nI\'ve discovered significant discrepancies in the Hindi textbooks. The previous dataset incorrectly listed NCERT Rimjhim chapters (\"\340\244\235\340\245\202\340\244\262\340\244\276,\" \"\340\244\206\340\244\256 \340\244\225\340\245\200 \340\244\225\340\244\271\340\244\276\340\244\250\340\245\200,\" etc.) for Class 1 and Class 2, when the official JCERT Jharkhand textbooks (\"\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 1\" and \"\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 2\") feature entirely different, Jharkhand-specific content. This critical error highlights a need to carefully cross-reference chapter titles and ensure data accuracy concerning the correct textbooks for each class.\n\n\n**Verifying Textbook Chapters**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing the Hindi textbook chapters for Class 1. I\'ve compiled the correct list: \"\340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\265\340\244\277\340\244\246\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\244\257,\" \"\340\244\206\340\244\210 \340\244\217\340\244\225 \340\244\226\340\244\274\340\244\254\340\244\260,\" \"\340\244\256\340\245\210\340\244\202 \340\244\255\340\245\200,\" \"\340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\270\340\245\200 \340\244\270\340\245\207 \340\244\225\340\244\271\340\244\250\340\244\276 \340\244\256\340\244\244,\" \"\340\244\260\340\244\270\340\245\213\340\244\210 \340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\202 \340\244\255\340\244\227\340\244\246\340\244\241\340\244\274,\" \"\340\244\250\340\244\237\340\244\226\340\244\237 \340\244\254\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\244\260,\" \"\340\244\256\340\245\210\340\244\241\340\244\256 \340\244\234\340\245\200,\" \"\340\244\227\340\245\201\340\244\254\340\245\215\340\244\254\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\276,\" \"\340\244\256\340\244\234\340\244\274\340\245\207 \340\244\225\340\245\200 \340\244\254\340\244\276\340\244\244,\" \"\340\244\270\340\244\260\340\244\271\340\245\201\340\244\262,\" \"\340\244\212\340\244\201\340\244\237 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\270\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\260,\" and \"\340\244\271\340\244\276\340\244\201 \340\244\234\340\245\200, \340\244\250\340\244\276...\". This confirms the previously noted discrepancies. The mathematics textbook is \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244\".\n\n\n**Compiling Math Textbook Chapters**\n\nNow, I\'m compiling the specific chapters for the Class 1 and Class 2 mathematics textbooks, \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 1\" and \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 2\" respectively, as part of this ongoing verification. For Class 1, I\'ve outlined chapters on comparisons, numbers, addition, subtraction, shapes, time, and patterns. Class 2 focuses on shapes, lines and numbers. This is a crucial step to compare the mathematics content as well.\n\n\n**Listing Math Textbook Chapters**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the math textbook chapters. I have documented chapters from \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 3\" for Class 3. The chapters cover concepts like place value, addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, time, measurement, fractions, and geometry. I\'m focusing on systematically mapping the math curriculum now.\n\n\n**Cataloging Math Chapters**\n\nI\'ve just finished documenting the mathematics chapters for \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 4\" and \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 5\". For Class 4, I\'ve listed chapters on shapes, large numbers, and money. Class 5 focuses on geometry, fractions, and data representation. I am now compiling this information to ensure the curriculum is complete and accurate.\n\n\n**Detailing Math Chapters**\n\nI\'ve just finished outlining the mathematics curriculum for Class 6, focusing on \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 6.\" This catalog includes chapters on geometry (points, lines, angles), numbers (place value, expanded form), operations, fractions, decimals, measurement (metric system), area and perimeter, time and speed, data analysis and patterns.\n\n**Documenting English Chapters**\n\nI am now documenting the English curriculum for \"Sunrise - 1,\" the Class 1 English textbook. So far, I\'ve listed the initial units: \"I Know,\" \"Myself,\" \"My Daily Routine,\" \"My Friend,\" \"My Food,\" and \"My House.\" I\'ll continue to fill in the remaining units.\n\n\n**Listing English Chapters**\n\nI\'ve just finished documenting additional English chapters. For \"Sunrise - 1,\" I\'ve listed Units 7 through 11. I am now documenting the English curriculum for \"Sunrise - 2.\" I am now focusing on English chapters in Sunshine - 3 and Sunshine - 4.\n\n\n**Cataloging English Chapters**\n\nI\'ve just documented \"Sunshine - 5\", the Class 5 English textbook. I\'ve finished outlining the chapters: \"Good Night and Good Morning,\" \"A Blind Child Speaks,\" \"My Nation,\" \"Save the World,\" \"The Swing,\" \"Mud on the Nose,\" \"Our Friend: Computer,\" \"Peace, Love, and Harmony,\" and \"Our Culture, Our Pride.\"\n\n\n**Outlining EVS Chapters**\n\nNow, I\'m documenting the Environmental Studies chapters for Classes 3 and 4. I\'ve listed chapters for \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 1,\" including \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\207 \340\244\205\340\244\252\340\244\250\340\245\207,\" \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\252\340\244\260\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\265\340\244\260\340\244\243,\" and \"\340\244\246\340\245\207\340\244\226\340\245\207-\340\244\205\340\244\250\340\244\246\340\245\207\340\244\226\340\245\207 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\250\340\244\265\340\244\260,\" for Class 3. I\'m also starting to outline chapters for \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 2\". I am ensuring the content covers the required topics.\n\n\n**Mapping EVS Chapters**\n\nI\'m now outlining \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 3\" from Class 5, which encompasses topics like heredity, family, migration and displacement. I\'ve finished listing the first three chapters for this textbook. I am meticulously reviewing each chapter\'s focus.\n\nI\'m also working on detailing how these concepts are addressed.\n\n\n**Listing EVS Chapters**\n\nI\'m presently documenting Environmental Studies chapters from the \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276\" series. I\'ve compiled the chapters for \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 4\", focusing on topics like shelters, animal senses, food preservation, seeds, and digestion. I\'ve also listed chapter 1 from \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 3\", focusing on the topic \"\340\244\260\340\245\207\340\244\262\340\244\227\340\244\276\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\245\200\". I am now focusing on the curriculum.\n\n\n**Listing Hindi Chapters**\n\nI\'ve just documented the Hindi chapters for \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 3\", which focuses on chapters like \"\340\244\270\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\270 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\262\340\245\213\340\244\256\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\245\200\" and \"\340\244\252\340\245\207\340\244\241\340\244\274.\" I have also documented \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 4\". The chapters include poetry and stories covering a variety of topics. I\'m ensuring I capture the breadth of the content.\n\n\n**Cataloging Hindi Chapters**\n\nI\'ve just documented the Hindi chapters from \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 5\". These include a diverse range of stories and poems such as \"\340\244\271\340\244\256 \340\244\270\340\244\254 \340\244\270\340\245\201\340\244\256\340\244\250 \340\244\217\340\244\225 \340\244\211\340\244\252\340\244\265\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\245\207,\" \"\340\244\210\340\244\246\340\244\227\340\244\276\340\244\271,\" \"\340\244\254\340\244\277\340\244\260\340\244\270\340\244\276 \340\244\256\340\245\201\340\244\202\340\244\241\340\244\276,\" and \"\340\244\252\340\245\215\340\244\260\340\244\225\340\245\203\340\244\244\340\244\277 \340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\270\340\244\226\340\245\200: \340\244\235\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\226\340\244\202\340\244\241,\" among others. I\'m focusing on the diversity and cultural richness of the textbook.\n\n\n**Listing EVS Chapters**\n\nI\'m presently documenting Environmental Studies chapters. I have just confirmed the final chapters in \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 5,\" including those focusing on ecosystems and resources. I\'ve also verified the list for \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 4\" and \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 5.\" Now, I\'m checking the subjects configured in `curriculum.ts` and their corresponding UI elements.\n\n\n**Verifying Subject Availability**\n\nI\'m now verifying the subjects available for each class in the JCERT curriculum. I\'ve confirmed that Class 1 comprises Maths (\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 1), Hindi (\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 1), and English (Sunrise - 1). Class 2 includes Maths (\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 2), Hindi (\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 2), and English (Sunrise - 2). Additionally, Class 3 has Maths (\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 3), Hindi (\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 3), English (Sunshine - 3), and EVS (\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 1).\n\n\n"
