ith our existing data.\n\n\n**Verifying Class 4 Content**\n\nI\'m currently working to confirm the Class 4 materials. Specifically, I\'m now mapping the chapters in \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 4\" and \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 4\". In math, I\'m ensuring chapters like \"Geometric Shapes,\" \"Large Numbers,\" and \"Time & Calendar\" match precisely. For Hindi, I\'ve confirmed \"Koyal\" and \"Bahubhashi Vidwan.\" I\'m prioritizing the precise alignment of names and order.\n\n\n**Checking Class 4 Hindi**\n\nI am now meticulously cross-referencing Class 4 Hindi and English content. I\'ve compiled the chapters from \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 4\", focusing on \"Papa Jab Bachhe The\" and its related content. I am now matching \"Mujhe Monitor Bana Do\" through \"Bijuka.\" Concurrently, I\'m ensuring \"Sunshine - 4\" aligns perfectly, specifically the chapters like \"The Stars & Sky and Her Children\" and onwards, to assure accuracy in every detail.\n\n\n**Matching Class 2 EVS**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the Environmental Studies chapters for Class 2, specifically \"Hamari Duniya - 2\". I am ensuring the chapters align, from \"Chalo Chalen School\" to \"Hu Tu Tu\". I\'m cross-referencing to ensure precise title, topic, and number. My immediate focus is this alignment of details with JCERT Jharkhand textbook.\n\n\n**Mapping Class 5 Content**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing Class 5\'s \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 5\" textbook against our existing data. I\'ve compiled the chapters: \"Geometry,\" \"Numbers & Place Values,\" \"Large Addition & Subtraction,\" and \"Multiplication & Division.\" My immediate focus is to get each chapter name and topic to perfectly mirror the original text. I\'m focusing on verifying the exact wording, especially on the early Math chapters.\n\n\n**Listing Class 5 Details**\n\nI am now organizing Class 5 materials, beginning with math, with topics like \"Data & Bar Graphs\" and \"Patterns\". Moving on, I have started with Hindi, mapping \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 5\". I\'ve compiled a full chapter list, starting with \"Hum Sab Suman Ek Upvan Ke\" and continuing through \"Hockey Ka Jaadugar.\" My priority is absolute accuracy.\n\n\n**Verifying Class 5 Content**\n\nI\'m currently working to confirm the accuracy of Class 5\'s data. I\'ve now listed the chapters for \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 5,\" including \"Rani Lakshmibai\" and \"Prakriti Meri Sakhi: Jharkhand.\" For English, \"Sunshine - 5\" has also been compiled, from \"Good Night and Good Morning\" to \"Mother Teresa.\" My current focus is to verify that these chapters perfectly reflect the original Jharkhand textbooks.\n\n\n**Aligning Class 3 EVS**\n\nI\'m now carefully mapping the Environmental Studies chapters for Class 3, focusing on \"Hamari Duniya - 3.\" I\'ve meticulously listed \"\340\244\225\340\245\214\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\270\340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\234\340\245\210\340\244\270\340\244\276\" through \"\340\244\225\340\245\210\340\244\270\340\245\207-\340\244\225\340\245\210\340\244\270\340\245\207 \340\244\230\340\244\260\". I\'m cross-referencing to confirm the exact topic, title, and number alignment with the Jharkhand JCERT textbook. Accuracy is my priority as I verify each detail for the final check.\n\n\n**Confirming Language Requirements**\n\nI\'ve just added chapters 11 and 12 from \"Hamari Duniya - 3\" for Class 3. The list is complete for that class, and I\'m ensuring everything matches the JCERT Jharkhand curriculum. Now, I\'m shifting to ensuring that the three language requirements are fully satisfied, including the script options. I\'m focusing on ensuring all content supports each required language perfectly.\n\n\n**Implementing Font Support**\n\nI\'m now implementing the required Unicode fonts. Specifically, I\'m integrating Ol Chiki and Warang Chiti fonts to render Santali and Ho scripts accurately. My focus now is ensuring proper display of both scripts. I\'m prioritizing complete script functionality for each chapter.\n\n\n**Updating Subject Titles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying the correct subject names and JCERT textbook titles in `SubjectSelector.tsx`. I\'ve confirmed the subject mapping for each class, including: Class 1 (Maths: \340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 1, Hindi: \340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 1, English: Sunrise - 1), Class 2, Class 3, Class 4, and Class 5. The priority is accurate display.\n\n\n**Refining Subject Selector**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the `SubjectSelector.tsx` component. I\'m investigating the best way to handle different subjects per class. I\'m currently assessing the data structure in `src/data/curriculum.ts` and considering a helper function like `getSubjectsForClass(classNumber: number)` to dynamically render subject cards. I plan to display the correct book titles for each subject and class, ensuring the correct textbook titles like \"\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 1\" are displayed. My focus is streamlined subject selection.\n\n\n**Finalizing Data Presentation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final display elements. I\'ll ensure textbook names are shown at the top of the chapter maps, such as \"Class 2 \342\200\242 \340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 2 (JCERT Jharkhand).\" I also intend to add a badge to indicate \"Official JCERT Jharkhand Textbook\" and display the chapter count. In each