  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Component Interactions**\n\nI\'m now looking closely at the interaction between `SubjectSelector.tsx` and `ChapterMap.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m analyzing how `getSubjectsForClass(selectedClass)` behaves. For Class 1, I expect it to return a map including \'maths\': \340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 1, and \'hindi\': \340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 1.\n\n\n**Mapping Subject Availability**\n\nNow, I\'m defining the subject maps for Classes 2 through 5. Each class has specific subjects: Class 2 gets Maths, Hindi, and English; Class 3 adds EVS. Class 4 and 5 follow a similar pattern. Also, when changing classes, if the selected subject becomes invalid (like \'evs\' for Class 1), I\'ll reset the selected subject to a valid one, to ensure the user doesn\'t get stuck.\n\n\n**Validating App State**\n\nI\'m now focusing on `App.tsx` and `ClassSelector.tsx` to validate the state management. Specifically, when `selectedClass` updates to 1 or 2 and `selectedSubject` is \'evs\', I\'ll update it to \'maths\' to maintain a valid state. This prevents any empty state, which is great! Next, I\'ll move on to `LessonView.tsx` to handle chapters with empty `lessonSlides`. If `slides.length === 0`, I\'ll generate a default rich interactive slide with chapter details, ensuring that every JCERT chapter has an engaging lesson.\n\n\n**Constructing Curriculum Data**\n\nI\'m now building full curriculum files for each class: `curriculumClass1.ts`, `curriculumClass2.ts`, `curriculumClass3.ts`, `curriculumClass4.ts`, and `curriculumClass5.ts`. I will combine these into a `curriculum.ts` file. To ensure accuracy, I\'m re-verifying the chapters for all five classes, starting with the chapters in \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 1\" from Class 1.\n\n\n**Cataloging Lesson Content**\n\nI am now cataloging the lesson content for Class 1. I\'ve broken down \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 1\", \"\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 1\", and \"Sunrise - 1\" into individual lessons and chapters. This provides a detailed overview of what\'s covered in each book, including the precise order of Hindi lessons: \"\340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\252\340\244\260\340\244\277\340\244\232\340\244\257 / \340\244\252\340\245\215\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\215\340\244\245\340\244\250\340\244\276\", \"\340\244\230\340\245\213-\340\244\230\340\245\213 \340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\250\340\245\200\", and others. I\'m also ensuring all lessons are accounted for.\n\n\n**Defining Lesson Outlines**\n\nI\'m now detailing the lesson outlines for \"\340\244\260\340\245\213\340\244\232\340\244\225 \340\244\227\340\244\243\340\244\277\340\244\244 - 2\" (JCERT Class 2), specifically. I\'m noting each chapter, from \"\340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276 \340\244\271\340\245\210 \340\244\262\340\244\202\340\244\254\340\244\276, \340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276 \340\244\271\340\245\210 \340\244\227\340\245\213\340\244\262?\" to \"\340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\244\340\244\250\340\245\200 \340\244\232\340\245\213\340\244\237\340\245\200 \340\244\271\340\245\210\340\244\202?\". This ensures a clear structure for the second grade mathematics content, allowing for easy navigation and lesson planning.\n\n\n**Listing Curriculum Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the curriculum components for Class 2, specifically for Hindi (\"\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 2\") and English (\"Sunrise - 2\"). This is a meticulous process, but now I\'m listing all the lessons in each book to ensure completeness. For the \"\340\244\235\340\244\277\340\244\262\340\244\256\340\244\277\340\244\262 - 2\" text, I\'m identifying chapters like \"\340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\265\340\244\277\340\244\246\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\262\340\244\257\" and \"\340\244\250\340\244\237\340\244\226\340\244\237 \340\244\254\340\244\250\340\245\215\340\244\246\340\244\260\", and similarly for English, where I\'m logging lessons like \"My Family\" and \"The Pumpkin and the Cucumber.\"\n\n\n**Analyzing Lesson Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing a specific lesson for \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 3\" (JCERT Class 3) - the lesson is \"Railgadi\". I am also recording the lesson plan including the lessons listed above. This includes chapters like, \"Kanjoos\" and \"O Meri Machhli\" among the other lessons. I am keeping a meticulous approach to detail to ensure each chapter is correct.\n\n\n**Cataloging Lesson Content**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the lesson content for \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 3\" (JCERT Class 3) and \"Sunshine - 3\". For \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 3\", I\'m listing lessons such as \"\340\244\270 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\262\340\245\213\340\244\256\340\244\241\340\244\274\340\245\200 (Saaras aur Lomdi)\", \"\340\244\252\340\245\207\340\244\241\340\244\274 (Ped)\", \"\340\244\237\340\245\213\340\244\225\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\202 \340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276 \340\244\271\340\245\210 (Tokri Me Kya Hai)\", and \"\340\244\232\340\244\202\340\244\246\340\244\276 \340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\256\340\244\276 \340\244\225\340\245\201\340\244\217\340\244\201 \340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\202 (Chanda Mama Kuyen Me)\". For \"Sunshine - 3\", I am recording \"Unit 1: My Dear One & Hand Washing Day\", \"Unit 2: Old McDonald Had A Farm & Androcles and the Lion\" and other lessons.\n\n\n**Listing Curriculum Details**\n\nI am now detailing the curriculum for Class 3\'s EVS book, \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 1\". I\'m methodically listing each chapter, from \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\207 \340\244\205\340\244\252\340\244\250\340\245\207 (Our Near & Dear Ones)\" to \"\340\244\226\340\245\207\340\244\262 \340\244\224\340\244\260 \340\244\256\340\244\250\340\245\213\340\244\260\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\250 (Games & Festivals),\" ensuring comprehensive coverage. I\'m also cataloging the \"Sunshine - 3\" lessons: \"Soldiers & Veer Budhu Bhagat\", \"We Are Indians & Our Country\", and others.\n\n\n**Structuring Class 4 Content**\n\nI\'m now outlining the Class 4 curriculum, meticulously organizing math chapters like \"Geometric Shapes & Angles\" and \"Numbers,\" up to \"Data Representation.\" Then, I\'m cataloging \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 4\", with lessons such as \"Koyal\" and \"Mujhe Monitor Bana Do.\" This ensures a structured and organized approach to the lesson plan.\n\n\n**Organizing Lesson Outlines**\n\nI\'m now outlining the chapters for \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 2\" (JCERT Class 4\'s EVS book), listing chapters like \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\255\340\245\213\340\244\234\340\244\250 (Our Food)\", \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\206\340\244\265\340\244\276\340\244\270 (Our Home)\", and \"\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\250\340\245\200 (Water).\" Next, I\'m cataloging \"Sunshine - 4\", focusing on lessons such as \"The Stars & Sky and Her Children\", \"Frogs at School & The Clever Fishes\", and beyond. I\'m keeping a very precise and organized structure for the content.\n\n\n**Cataloging Lesson Content**\n\nI\'m now detailing the lesson outlines for \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 3\" (JCERT Class 5), including chapters on \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\244\276 \340\244\252\340\244\260\340\245\215\340\244\257\340\244\276\340\244\265\340\244\260\340\244\243 (Our Environment),\" \"\340\244\206\340\244\270-\340\244\252\340\244\276\340\244\270 \340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\234\340\244\276\340\244\250\340\244\265\340\244\260 (Animals Around Us),\" and beyond. Then, I\'m listing lessons from \"Sunshine - 5\", for example, \"The Selfish Giant\" and \"The Nightingale and the Rose\" among others. I\'m taking a very structured approach to the content for an organized structure.\n\n\n**Structuring Lesson Concepts**\n\nI\'m now outlining the Math concepts for Class 5, covering topics from Multiplication and Division to Patterns. Concurrently, I\'ve listed the Hindi lessons from \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 5,\" including \"Hum Sab Suman Ek Upvan Ke,\" \"Faslon Ka Tyohar,\" and others. This ensures comprehensive coverage of all aspects of the curriculum.\n\n\n\n**Listing Lesson Content**\n\nI\'m now cataloging \"\340\244\255\340\244\276\340\244\267\340\244\276\340\244\202\340\244\234\340\244\262\340\244\277 - 5\" and \"Sunshine - 5\" lessons. I\'ve listed Hindi lessons like \"\340\244\256\340\245\207\340\244\260\340\245\207 \340\244\252\340\245\215\340\244\260\340\244\245\340\244\256 \340\244\266\340\244\277\340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\267\340\244\225 (Mere Pratham Shikshak),\" \"\340\244\254\340\244\277\340\244\260\340\244\270\340\244\276 \340\244\256\340\245\201\340\244\202\340\244\241\340\244\276 (Birsa Munda),\" and \"\340\244\260\340\244\276\340\244\250\340\245\200 \340\244\262\340\244\225\340\245\215\340\244\267\340\245\215\340\244\256\340\245\200\340\244\254\340\244\276\340\244\210 (Rani Lakshmibai).\" In \"Sunshine - 5\", I\'ve documented Unit 1, including \"Good Night and Good Morning\" and \"The Wooden Bowl\", alongside other units.\n\n\n**Detailing Lesson Coverage**\n\nI\'m now detailing the remaining \"Sunshine - 5\" units, encompassing \"Mud on the Nose,\" \"The Cricket Match,\" \"Our Friend: Computer,\" and \"Peace, Love and Harmony.\" Finally, I\'ve listed \"Mother Teresa,\" \"Our Culture, Our Pride,\" and \"Flying High.\" Moving to \"\340\244\271\340\244\256\340\244\276\340\244\260\340\245\200 \340\244\246\340\245\201\340\244\250\340\244\277\340\244\257\340\244\276 - 3\" (Class 5 EVS), I\'m cataloging lessons like \"\340\244\225\340\245\214\340\244\250 \340\244\225\340\244\277\340\244\270\340\244\225\340\245\207 \340\244\234\340\245\210\340\244\270\340\244\276,\" \"\340\244\225\340\244\276\340\244\256 \340\244\225\340\245\200 \340\244\226\340\245\213\340\244\234,\" and \"\340\244\254\340\244\246\340\244\262\340\244\276 \340\244\254\340\244\270\340\245\207\340\244\260\340\244\276\" to build complete coverage. The process continues in a methodical fashion.\n\n\n"
